---
description: Next.js frontend implementation quality rules for Ball Takes
alwaysApply: false
globs: "**/*.{tsx,ts,jsx,js,css,scss}"
---
- Inspect installed Next.js/React versions and router before using version-specific APIs.
- Prefer server-rendered/read-heavy UI where supported; use client components only for interaction/browser needs.
- Avoid client request waterfalls; fetch independent data concurrently where practical.
- Reserve image/media dimensions to reduce layout shift and lazy-load below-fold media.
- Prefer next/image where appropriate and compatible with the media source.
- Do not add a UI or animation library until existing dependencies have been evaluated.
- Keep mobile layouts intentional; do not merely shrink desktop multi-column layouts.
- Run repository lint/typecheck/tests/build after implementation phases.
